# D-TASK-SLICE1=A: a task busy in a loop that never waits still stops on
# time, at the check its next iteration starts with. `task.any` returns 7
# although its other branch only computes; `task.all` fails fast on a
# branch whose assert stops it while its other branch only computes; and a
# busy task's `#Deadline(20ms)` block stops it with the deadline failure
# after its deferred close runs. Without the delivery the combinators and the
# join never return and the steps time out. task.race and the plain cancel
# are a_cancel_or_deadline_stops_a_busy_loop_at_its_next_iteration_on_every_tier.
fixture: any_all_and_a_deadline_block_stop_a_busy_task_on_every_tier.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\n0\nclose the handler's marker\nthe handler: deadline\n"
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\n0\nclose the handler's marker\nthe handler: deadline\n"
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\n0\nclose the handler's marker\nthe handler: deadline\n"
step: jet build -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
step aot: built
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\n0\nclose the handler's marker\nthe handler: deadline\n"
